course: dictionary
lesson: 3109
title: Words that stretch and spring back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Elastic» is a word that describes something that stretches when you pull it and then goes back to its usual shape. You can use it as a noun, for the material itself, or as an adjective, for things that can stretch. The waist of your trousers may have elastic in it, so it can stretch to go over your hips and then hold them up.
explain: Scientists test elastic things in lessons on forces. They pull a rubber band or a spring, see how far it stretches, and then let go to watch it return. The pull is the force, and the band's ability to spring back is its elasticity.
explain: Read the context to work out the meaning. «The chameleon's tongue is released like a stretched elastic band.» A band that is stretched and let go snaps back, so you can guess that elastic means able to stretch and spring back. Then check: does the idea of a stretched band snapping back fit the sentence? It does.
explain: Words can have different meanings in different languages. In Chinese, «tiào píjīn» is the word for elastics, a game played with a stretched band. The sound is different, but the idea of stretching and springing is still there.
fact: Elastic means able to stretch when pulled and then go back to its normal shape.
fact: Elastic is also a noun for the stretchy material, such as the elastic in a waistband.
fact: An elastic band is a rubber band.
fact: «A chameleon's tongue shoots out to about twice its body length in a fraction of a second.» The tongue works like a stretched elastic band, with a sticky cup at the tip.
fact: In Chinese, «tiào shéng» means skipping with a rope, and «tiào píjīn» means elastics.
exercise: «The chameleon's tongue is released like a stretched elastic band.» What does elastic mean here? | Made of wood and very hard | *Able to stretch and spring back | Very heavy and slow | Sticky and cold
exercise: Mum sewed «elastic» into the waist of my trousers. What is elastic? | *A stretchy material that goes back to its shape | Paint for painting walls | A hard metal used for pipes | A kind of bread
exercise: «The rubber was very elastic, so it bounced back.» Find and copy one word that tells you the rubber could stretch. | rubber | back | bounced | *elastic
test: In a science lesson, you pull a rubber band and let go. Why is it called elastic? | It breaks as soon as it is pulled | It melts in your hand | It is always cold to touch | *It stretches and springs back to its shape
test: What is an elastic band? | A steel bar used in buildings | A very tall tree | A kind of song | *A rubber band
exam: Which word means a stretchy material that goes back to its shape, as in trousers with a waistband? | plastic | metal | *elastic | wool
